high-level-scenarios.S5:
baseline-from-before-file — file `/path/to/doc.md` opened;
`/path/to/doc.md.before` exists and is readable; baseline loaded
from .before file; BLOCK_BASELINE_LOADED source=file path=...before.

high-level-scenarios.S10:
auto-detect-before-file — open doc.md where doc.md.before exists;
diff mode activated automatically; BLOCK_AUTO_DIFF_TRIGGERED; user
can dismiss via Cmd+D or toolbar close button.

failure-scenarios.F3:
git-not-available — git binary not installed or not in PATH;
`std::process::Command` returns io::Error NotFound; fallback to
.before-file-only resolution; if .before also missing, F1 path;
BLOCK_GIT_UNAVAILABLE reason=binary_not_found.

race-conditions.R2:
external-change-while-diff-open — notify-debouncer (V-M-003) fires
file-changed event while diff view is active; current content
updated from disk; diff view re-diffs against same baseline;
MergeView.setValue() triggers incremental re-render;
BLOCK_DIFF_REFRESHED trigger=external_change.

race-conditions.R6:
concurrent-baseline-requests — multiple tabs opened simultaneously
with .before files (e.g., session restore); each invokes
mt_diff_baseline independently; Rust handler is stateless per-call;
no shared mutable state; concurrent execution safe;
BLOCK_BASELINE_LOADED carries tab_id for correlation.

numeric-thresholds.T5:
Baseline fetch latency: .before file ≤50ms for ≤1MB file; git show
≤200ms for ≤1MB file in repo with ≤10K commits;
BLOCK_BASELINE_FETCH_ELAPSED_MS.

high-level-scenarios.S3:
cursor-preservation — file has 100 lines, cursor at line 50;
external edit appends 3 lines at end; after reload, cursor restored
to line 50 (saved before Object.assign, restored after).

high-level-scenarios.S4:
scroll-preservation — editor scrolled to middle; external edit
changes first paragraph; scrollTop value preserved across reload;
viewport doesn't jump.

high-level-scenarios.S5:
dirty-conflict — user has unsaved edits (isSaved=false); external
write fires; notification shown with "Reload / Keep mine";
user choice respected. BLOCK_RELOAD_CONFLICT action=user_choice.

high-level-scenarios.S6:
save-echo-suppression — user saves file; watcher detects our write;
hash compare finds no diff; reload skipped. BLOCK_RELOAD_SKIPPED
reason=no_diff.

high-level-scenarios.S7:
file-deleted-externally — watcher fires kind="remove";
APPLY_FILE_CHANGE('unlink', ...) shows "File
removed" banner; content kept in memory. (Already works.)

high-level-scenarios.S8:
liveReload-pref-off — user sets liveReload=false in preferences;
external change triggers notification (old behavior) instead of
auto-reload.

failure-scenarios.F2:
invalid-utf8 — external tool writes binary/Latin-1 content; Rust
mt::fs::read returns error (read_to_string fails on non-UTF8);
catch; keep old content; toast error.

high-level-scenarios.S4:
preview-click-exits — user left-clicks in preview content;
handlePreviewMousedown fires; exits preview mode → enters edit mode
(existing behavior from M-022).

race-conditions.R1:
file-deleted-during-preview — file deleted while preview open;
watcher fires "remove"; banner "File removed";
content stays in memory; preview remains read-only.

edge-cases.E4:
discovery-empty-directory — extension directory exists but contains
no subdirectories; mt_ext_discover returns empty list;
BLOCK_EXT_DISCOVER count=0.

edge-cases.E5:
discovery-directory-missing — extension directory does not exist;
mt_ext_discover creates it and returns empty list;
BLOCK_EXT_DISCOVER count=0 created_dir=true.
